<title>SPAIN: Spain Sept CPI rose 0.2 pct, yr/yr 3.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain Sept CPI rose 0.2 pct, yr/yr 3.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute (INE) gave the following figures:</p>
<p> SPANISH INFLATION		SEPT 96    AUG 96    SEPT 95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change	0.2	  0.3	 0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 3.6	  3.7	 4.4</p>
<p> Core inflation		    0.2	  0.2	 0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 3.4	  3.6	 4.9</p>
<p> INDEX BY COMPONENTS	     SEPT 96    AUG 96     YR/YR</p>
<p> Food				    0.2	 0.7	   4.0</p>
<p> Clothing				0.2	 0.0	   2.7</p>
<p> Housing				 0.4	 0.2	   4.1</p>
<p> Household goods		     0.2	 0.0	   4.1</p>
<p> Medicine				0.1	 0.0	   3.5</p>
<p> Transport			     0.1	 0.2	   3.1</p>
<p> Culture				 0.7	 0.0	   2.8</p>
<p> Other				   0.2	 0.1	   3.7</p>
<p>Note - In food, fresh food rose 0.5 pct from the previous month (3.9 pct year-on-year) and processed food rose 0.0 (4.0 pct year-on-year)</p>
</text>
